The c-icap server                         http://c-icap.sourceforge.net/

c-icap is an implementation of an ICAP server. It can be used with HTTP
proxies that support the ICAP protocol to implement content adaptation
and filtering services.

Most of the commercial HTTP proxies must support the ICAP protocol. The
open source Squid proxy server supports it.

Major features:
  - ICAP over TLS support
  - C API for developing custom content adaptation and filtering services
  - plugins interface
  - LDAP integration
  - simple ICAP client API

For support, use the following resources:
 - General discussion related to c-icap server:
   c-icap-users@lists.sourceforge.net
 - Basic installation and configuration instructions:
   https://sourceforge.net/p/c-icap/wiki/configcicap/
 - c-icap service developers should start from here:
   https://sourceforge.net/p/c-icap/wiki/Developers/

## TSNLab

### How to run?
```Bash
sudo apt-get install c-icap build-essential autoconf automake libtool libbrotli-dev libz-dev libbz2-dev

git clone https://github.com/tsnlab/c-icap-server
cd c-icap-server
autoreconf -i
./configure
cd services/tsnlab_echo # Example
make
ls .libs/tsnlab_echo.so
cp .libs/tsnlab_echo.so /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/c_icap/ # x86 Ubuntu 24.04
```

#### C-ICAP Server Config
```Bash
# sudo vi /etc/c-icap/c-icap.conf

Service tsnlab_echo tsnlab_echo.so
```

#### Squid Proxy Server Config
```Bash
# sudo vi /etc/squid/squid.conf

# ICAP Server Enable
icap_enable on
icap_send_client_ip on
icap_send_client_username on

# ICAP Server Address Configuration (ICAP Default Port 1344)
icap_service service_tsnlab_req reqmod_precache icap://localhost:1344/tsnlab_echo
icap_service service_tsnlab_resp respmod_precache icap://localhost:1344/tsnlab_echo

# Service Registration (All Traffic)
adaptation_access service_tsnlab_req allow all
adaptation_access service_tsnlab_resp allow all
```
